{# The assistant, shared by its two surfaces (ARCHITECTURE.md §8.87): the
   help panel's third state, and the /aide/assistant page. One partial,
   one endpoint, one script — two copies of a conversation would drift on
   the day one of them gained a state the other did not.

   Nothing here is rendered by the server except the shell: the exchanges
   arrive from POST /api/aide/assistant and are built by
   public/assets/js/help-assistant.js, node by node. The answer is a
   model's output, so it is escaped server-side by MarkdownRenderer before
   it ever gets here.

   Parameters:
   - available   whether the connector is operational (the assistant is
                 offered at all)
   - compact     true inside the panel, false on the full page. The panel
                 gets NO field of its own: it already has the search box,
                 and « Demander à l'assistant » sends what is typed there
                 straight away. Two boxes one under the other on the same
                 screen is the thing a reader cannot make sense of — which
                 one searches? which one asks? — so there is one.

   data-* only, no inline handlers (CSP — design.md §7.5). #}
{% set available = available|default(false) %}
{% set compact = compact|default(false) %}

<div class="help-assistant" data-help-assistant>
    {% if not available %}
        {# The degraded state that is not an error: this site has no AI
           provider configured, which is a normal way for a unit to run.
           Say what still works rather than what does not. #}
        <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
            L'assistant n'est pas disponible sur ce site : il demande qu'un fournisseur
            d'intelligence artificielle soit configuré. La recherche dans l'aide,
            elle, fonctionne toujours — y compris hors connexion.
        </p>
    {% else %}
        {# Named, because an unlabelled stack of question-and-answer
           blocks reads as "something the page decided to show me". It is
           a conversation, it is yours, and it does not outlive your
           visit — all three are worth one line. Revealed by
           help-assistant.js with the first exchange. #}
        <div class="d-none" data-help-assistant-history>
            <h3 class="h6 fw-semibold mb-1">Vos échanges avec l'assistant</h3>
            <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-2">
                Ils disparaissent à votre déconnexion : rien n'est conservé.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-3" data-help-assistant-thread aria-live="polite"></div>

        {# Offline, the exchange cannot happen: the answer comes from a
           provider on the internet. offline-nav.js intercepts the POST and
           opens its own dialog, and this line says so before the visitor
           types a paragraph for nothing. #}
        <p class="small text-body-secondary d-none" data-help-assistant-offline>
            <i class="bi bi-wifi-off" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            Vous êtes hors connexion. L'assistant a besoin d'internet ;
            la recherche ci-dessus fonctionne sans.
        </p>

        {% if not compact %}
            {# Only on the full page, where this is the ONLY field. In the
               panel the search box above does this job. #}
            <form data-help-assistant-form>
                <label for="help-assistant-question" class="visually-hidden">
                    Votre question pour l'assistant
                </label>
                <div class="input-group">
                    <input type="text" class="form-control"
                           id="help-assistant-question"
                           name="question" autocomplete="off" maxlength="500"
                           placeholder="Posez votre question…"
                           data-help-assistant-input>
                    {# Emptying a long question by hand to type the next one
                       is the kind of small friction that stops people
                       asking a second one. Shown only when there is
                       something to clear. #}
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary d-none"
                            data-help-assistant-clear>
                        <i class="bi bi-x-lg" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span class="visually-hidden">Effacer la question</span>
                    </button>
                    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" data-help-assistant-submit>
                        <i class="bi bi-send" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span class="visually-hidden">Envoyer</span>
                    </button>
                </div>
            </form>
        {% endif %}

        <p class="form-text mb-0">
            L'assistant répond uniquement à partir des sujets d'aide de ce site. Il ne
            consulte jamais les données de votre unité.
        </p>
    {% endif %}
</div>
